// A constant may be shadowed, but only on purpose.
//
// Shalimar makes a name on first write, so 'pi : 3' with no declaration
// would leave '? pi' meaning 3.14159 above that line and 3 below it - one
// name with two meanings in one function. That is the hazard the language
// document named when it made pi and e read-only, and it is the half worth
// keeping. Declaring 'real pi' first says the shadowing was meant, and
// cases/shadowing.shm holds that.
fun <> = main() {
  ? pi
  pi : 3.0
  ? pi
  return
}
